<title>GERMANY: BASKETBALL- EUROLEAGUE MEN'S DRAW.</title>
<headline>BASKETBALL- EUROLEAGUE MEN'S DRAW.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Draw for the 1997-1998 EuroLeague</p>
<p>men's basketball competition made on Tuesday:</p>
<p>Group A</p>
<p>CSKA Moscow (Russia)</p>
<p>Efes Pilsen Istanbul (Turkey)</p>
<p>Limoges (France)</p>
<p>Maccabi Elite Tel Aviv (Israel)</p>
<p>Olympiakos (Greece)</p>
<p>Real Madrid (Spain)</p>
<p>Group B</p>
<p>Porto (Portugal)</p>
<p>Estudiantes Madrid (Spain)</p>
<p>Turk Telekom Ankara (Turkey)</p>
<p>Croatia  Split (Croatia)</p>
<p>Benetton Treviso (Italy)</p>
<p>PAOK Salonika (Greece)</p>
<p>Group C</p>
<p>Partizan Belgrade (Yugoslavia)</p>
<p>Pau-Orthez (France)</p>
<p>Kinder  Bologna (Italy)</p>
<p>Hapoel Jerusalem (Israel)</p>
<p>Barcelona  (Spain)</p>
<p>Ulker Spor (Turkey)</p>
<p>Group D</p>
<p>Alba Berlin (Germany)</p>
<p>AEK Athens (Greece)</p>
<p>Olimpija Ljubljana (Slovenia)</p>
<p>Cibona Zagreb (Croatia)</p>
<p>PSG Racing Basket Paris (France)</p>
<p>Teamsystem Bologna (Italy)</p>
<p>First phase September 18-February 19. Best four in each</p>
<p>group proceed to next stage with four clubs eventually</p>
<p>qualifying for the Final Four in Barcelona from April 21-23.</p>
</text>
